h":100.0,"_gate_shrhldr_yield":-0.036210156779079176,"_gp_shrhldr_yield":false,"_score_shrhldr_yield":0.0,"_gate_share_shrink":0.008508929617743632,"_gp_share_shrink":false,"_score_share_shrink":39.4,"_gate_sbc_dilution":0.009191316491049891,"_gp_sbc_dilution":true,"_score_sbc_dilution":84.7,"_gate_insider_own":0.00526,"_gp_insider_own":false,"_score_insider_own":3.5,"_gate_insider_buying":0.067,"_gp_insider_buying":false,"_score_insider_buying":6.7,"pf":[],"description_full":"ITT Inc., together with its subsidiaries, manufactures and sells engineered critical components and customized technology solutions for the transportation, industrial, and energy markets. The company operates three segments: Motion Technologies, Industrial Process, and Connect & Control Technologies. The Motion Technologies segment manufactures brake pads, shock absorbers, energy absorption components, and damping technologies primarily for the transportation industry, including passenger cars, trucks, light and heavy-duty commercial and military vehicles, buses, and trains. This segment sells its products under the ITT Friction Technologies, KONI, Axtone, and Novitek brand names. The Industrial Process segment provides industrial pumps, valves, plant optimization, and remote monitoring systems and services; and aftermarket solutions, such as replacement parts and services. It serves various customers in the energy, chemical and petrochemical, pharmaceutical, general industrial, marine, mining, pulp and paper, food and beverage, power generation, and biopharmaceutical industries. This segment sells its products under the Goulds Pumps, Bornemann, Engineered Valves, Hamworthy Pumps, PRO Services, C'treat, Svaneh\u00f8j, Rheinh\u00fctte Pumpen, and Habonim brand names. The Connect & Control Technologies segment offers engineered connectors, cable assemblies, and specialized products for critical applications supporting various markets, including aerospace and defence, industrial, transportation, medical, and energy under the Cannon, VEAM, BIW Connector Systems, CIA&D, Compulink, Aerospace Controls, Enidine, Compact Automation, Charles E. Gillman, Turn-Act, Neo-Dyn, TopFlite Components, Conoflow, VIDAR, kSARIA, and Micro-Mode brand names. It operates in North America, Europe, Asia, the Middle East, Africa, and South America. The company was incorporated in 1920 and is headquartered in Stamford, Connecticut.","ceo_bio":"Mr. Luca  Savi | CEO, President & Director | Age 59 | Compensation: $4.0M (FY2016)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 11K people. Revenue per employee of $340K ranks in the below the sector median among Industrials peers, with revenue falling 6%/yr across its filed history. Each employee generates $47K of free cash flow annually. Stock-based compensation of $3K per employee reflects an ownership culture. CEO compensation is 12\u00d7 revenue per employee (reasonable relative to workforce productivity). Governance score flags low compensation governance risk (2/10).","financial_summary":["ITT Inc. is a large-cap industrials business with a $18.8B market cap on $3.9B of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at +10% over the past three years and +5% annually across the full decade, a respectable pace for a business of this size.","Returns on capital run at 19% against a 11% cost of capital \u2014 a 9-point spread that is the clearest signature of an economic moat, with gross margins sitting at 32%.","The business throws off $548M in free cash flow \u2014 roughly 14 cents on every revenue dollar, which is the owner-earnings figure that actually belongs to shareholders, and cash conversion sits at 1.37\u00d7 so those profits are backed by real cash.","On the balance sheet, the balance sheet carries net cash, which is the gold standard: the business never has to make desperate decisions in a bad year, and interest coverage of 14\u00d7 is fortress-like.","Net dilution runs at 3.6% annually, transferring value from owners to stock-based comp, and insider ownership is negligible, so management has little personal stake in the long-term outcome, and within its sector the business captures 1.6\u00d7 its fair share of profits, a structural advantage visible in the numbers."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Price sits 53% above estimated fair value \u2014 no margin of safety left, and the cushion against estimate error has been bid away (confirmed by 2 other valuation measures)","sev":"red","cat":"valuation","magnitude":0.526413353932656},{"text":"Volatile returns on capital suggest the moat is narrower than a snapshot ROIC implies","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Above-average short interest at 8.1% of float","sev":"amber","cat":"sentiment"},{"text":"Insiders are net sellers (93% sell ratio, net $12.9M) \u2014 the people closest to the business are reducing their personal stake","sev":"amber","cat":"insider"},{"text":"Industrials sector lagging the market significantly, underperforming by 6% over 3 months","sev":"amber","cat":"sector"},{"text":"Cyclicality and capital intensity \u2014 order books turn on a dime, and the heavy fixed cost base that creates the moat also magnifies the downturn.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Supply chain reshoring costs and labour shortages \u2014 onshoring mandates raise capex requirements while a shrinking skilled-labour pool inflates operating costs.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Tariff and trade-policy exposure \u2014 industrial exporters sit squarely in the crosshairs of protectionist policy, and retaliatory tariffs can close markets without warning.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["Reinvestment rate supports 19% organic growth capacity \u2014 capital is compounding inside the business","Operating margins 9% above sector median \u2014 the quantitative trace of pricing power","Altman Z comfortably in the safe zone \u2014 a fortress balance sheet on this measure","30 consecutive years of dividend payments \u2014 an operating record that makes the dividend claim credible","Healthy payout ratio leaves room for both dividend growth and reinvestment","Among the least levered in Industrials \u2014 the fortress balance sheet in its peer set"],"news_headlines":[{"title":"SSUMY or ITT: Which Is the Better Value Stock Right Now?","source":"zacks.com","link":"https://www.zacks.com/stock/news/3029692/ssumy-or-itt-which-is-the-better-value-stock-right-now?cid=CS-ZC-FT-fundamental_analysis%7Cyseop_template_3-3029692","date":"2026-11-13","timestamp":1794584404.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.649,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"ITT Inc. $ITT Stock: Pier 88 Investment Partners LLC Lowers Position","source":"thelincolnianonline.com","link":"https://www.thelincolnianonline.com/2026/11/13/itt-inc-itt-stock-pier-88-investment-partners-llc-lowers-position.html","date":"2026-11-13","timestamp":1794568332.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.691,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"Here's Why ITT (ITT) is a Strong Momentum Stock","source":"zacks.com","link":"https://www.zacks.com/stock/news/3028119/here-s-why-itt-itt-is-a-strong-momentum-stock?cid=CS-ZC-FT-fundamental_analysis%7Czacks_education_momentum_score-3028119","date":"2026-11-11","timestamp":1794428236.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.511,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"3 Reasons Why Growth Investors Shouldn't Overlook ITT (ITT)","source":"zacks.com","link":"https://www.zacks.com/stock/news/3027926/3-reasons-why-growth-investors-shouldn-t-overlook-itt-itt?cid=CS-ZC-FT-fundamental_analysis%7Cyseop_template_11_growth-3027926","date":"2026-11-11","timestamp":1794415502.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.382,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"Why ITT (ITT) is a Top Growth Stock for the Long-Term","source":"zacks.com","link":"https://www.zacks.com/stock/news/3027192/why-itt-itt-is-a-top-growth-stock-for-the-long-term?cid=CS-ZC-FT-fundamental_analysis%7Czacks_education_growth_score-3027192